4645822929.body:
You are right. At the commit you reviewed, `check_pv` reads only rows 0..group_heads-1 of `o_amx` [t/t_amx_numerics.cpp:275], and the production loop reads only rows 0..kv_mul-1 of `amx_o` [h/tron/models/self_attention.hpp:1792-1797]. So a P-fill bound of 16 rows [src/tron/kernels/amx_attn.cpp:271] would read 3 KiB past the 1024-byte `s_pages` [self_attention.hpp:1755] and no assertion would notice.

Done: your zero check is added, with one change. In the 4-head case the test's own `exp_rows` was also 4 rows [t/t_amx_numerics.cpp:260], so a regressed bound would have read the test's stack, and whether that garbage is nonzero is not deterministic. `exp_rows` now has 16 rows, and rows group_heads..15 hold 1.0f. The correct kernel never reads those rows, so the output rows stay exactly zero (zero P rows times V, Note [Tile stores write 16 rows]). A regressed bound turns each of them into the sum of 64 V values, nonzero for this seed, and the test stays in bounds.

```
  // Rows group_heads..15 hold a nonzero value the kernel must never read.
  constexpr float UNREAD_WEIGHT_1 = 1.f;
  alignas(64) float exp_rows[TILE_ROWS_16][PAGE_TOKENS_64];
  for (size_t qi = 0; qi < TILE_ROWS_16; ++qi) {
    for (auto& x : exp_rows[qi]) {
      x = qi < group_heads ? std::exp(ue(gen)) : UNREAD_WEIGHT_1;
    }
  }
  ...
  // Rows group_heads..15 of o_amx are zero P rows times V
  // (Note [Tile stores write 16 rows]).
  for (size_t qi = group_heads; qi < TILE_ROWS_16; ++qi) {
    for (size_t d = 0; d < HEAD_SIZE_128; ++d) {
      CAPTURE(qi, d);
      REQUIRE(o_amx[qi * HEAD_SIZE_128 + d] == 0.f);
    }
  }
```

The PV case skips without AMX, so I ran `t_amx_numerics` on a Granite Rapids host (delphi-3b35) at the final head. The 4-head PV section passes 2,561 assertions, and the 16-head section passes 4,097. The 4-head section's name is now "4 heads: rows 0..3 in the envelope, rows 4..15 zero".
